* kisi 0.3.3: lane BUS_P as a SPICE subcircuit (ngspice, Xyce, LTspice, KiCad)
* board board.kicad_pcb
* subcircuit BUS_P_lane (pair: P and N on their own paths, coupled sections in modal form)
* port 1 (ap): P BUS_P at U1.6 (transmitter end)
* port 2 (an): N BUS_N at U1.7 (transmitter end)
* port 3 (bp): P BUS_P at U2.6 (receiver end)
* port 4 (bn): N BUS_N at U2.7 (receiver end)
* track length 55.75 mm, delay 315.3 ps, reference 50.00 ohm per port
* model: kisi's channel sections; lines as RLGC ladders (20.00 sections per wavelength at 10.00 GHz) with fitted
*   Foster (R(f), L_int(f)) and Debye (G(f), C(f)) networks, vias as kisi's via ladder, parts with estimated
*   parasitics, open stubs; coupled sections of a pair as even/odd chains between ideal mode converters (E/F)
* check against kisi's S-parameters (same model): |dS21| <= 0.09911 dB to 1.5 x Nyquist (3.383 dB to the top), largest |dS| 0.01564 to 1.5 x Nyquist (0.4426 to the top)
* fits of the main line sections (each at least 10 % of the length): R 0.5148 %, X 0.03238 %, G 95.98 %, B 13.31 %; via ladders 0 %
* elements after flattening: 2218 R, 1586 L, 992 C, 80 sources; 164 RLGC sections
* usage: X1 ap an bp bn 0 BUS_P_lane   (the last port is the reference)
* stackup: 2 copper layers, 1.49 mm, er and tand at 1 GHz; from board file (layer by layer in the README)
*   layers (um): F.Cu 30 / 1430 er 4.42 tand 0.02 / B.Cu 30

